@startuml seq-rank-and-map
title UC-04 / UC-05 · Rank characters and show the route on the star map
skinparam shadowing false
actor User
participant "Browser UI\n(rank.js + map.js)" as UI
participant "Routes" as R
participant "RankingService" as RS
participant "GateGraph" as G
participant "LiveProvider" as P
participant "EsiClient" as E
participant "ESI" as ESI
database "SQLite" as DB

User -> UI : type target or paste message text
UI -> R : GET /api/systems/search or POST /api/target/resolve
R --> UI : candidate systems
UI -> R : GET /api/rank?target=Tama&refresh=1
R -> RS : rank(target, mode)
alt snapshots younger than 30 s (stale-while-revalidate)
  RS -> RS : answer from snapshots; start a background round if older than 5 s
else first ranking, or Refresh button (mode 2)
  RS -> P : fetch all enabled characters (one shared round, single flight)
  P -> E : location / ship / online (max 20 in parallel)
  E -> ESI : GET (skipped until Expires, If-None-Match)
  ESI --> E : 200 or 304
  RS -> DB : save_snapshots (one transaction)
end
RS -> G : bfs(target, avoid = [Zarzakh]) (cached per target)
G --> RS : parent pointers
RS -> RS : route per character, sort: reachable, jumps, online, name; mark Closest
RS --> UI : rows (jumps, system, ship, docked, route ids)
UI -> UI : list on the left, closest selected
UI -> UI : map.setScene(target, route, markers) - draw route, fit view
User -> UI : click another character
UI -> UI : draw that character's route (no server call)
@enduml
